import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.PeriodFamilyHolomorphicCohomologyCocycleVanishing

/-!
# Genuine native cohomology classes of a holomorphic period family

For every original holomorphic period map on a holomorphic base, this
package constructs native additive holomorphic cocycles from four
holomorphic coefficient functions. The actual local inverses of the
original quotient covering have sources covering the original total
space. Their primitive differences are locally the holomorphic
character of a fixed original lattice vector, proving holomorphicity
in the original varying-period atlas.

The construction has the fixed orientation `L_i - L_j` and maps into
the original holomorphic sheaf's genuine native first cohomology by
the actual extension class. It is additive and complex-linear for
the scalar action induced by the original scalar sheaf morphisms.
Characters obtained from holomorphic complex-linear forms on the
cover are actual holomorphic coboundaries, so their genuine native
cohomology classes vanish.

This is a construction of classes and their proved linear relations.
It makes no assertion of surjectivity, a frame for a higher direct
image, or a comparison with the native marking on an individual fibre.
-/
